From ba312c44848c3dbc691c3513cad1d5b63f606730 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 10:42:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: cross-origin isolation from COOP/COEP, CORP and COEP
 enforcement

The window's cross-origin isolated capability follows the top-level
document's opener policy (same-origin-plus-COEP) and the permissions
policy's cross-origin-isolated feature (default allowlist 'self', the
iframe allow attribute); an embedder may set the top-level value for a
traversable shown as a frame elsewhere. Policy containers from a fetch
response get their embedder policy (obtain an embedder policy). Fetch
runs the cross-origin resource policy check for opaque responses, nested
navigations run it with forNavigation and check the response's
adherence to the parent's embedder policy. Credentialless reads the
client's policy container. A frame's error page no longer needs the
resource template, and a module evaluation rejected in a realm without
a window is dropped instead of a VERIFY.
